-- title:
--   Residual transcendence of the supersingular valuation ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$, a nonzero $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a nonunit of $A$; write $\kappa=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$ over $\kappa$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in the supersingular set), let the base-changed full-level field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ be contained in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$ whose residue map is computed coefficientwise on Laurent series with coefficients in $A$, and fix $s\in W$. Fix further small-constant data: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that $A\cap k_0$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ and algebraically closed residue field, every element of $A$ being congruent modulo $\mathfrak m_A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$; a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\neq q$, $\ell\nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ that is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; and $\varpi_t\in k_0\cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Fix also an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ equal to $\bot$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ cut out by $A$, and a generator $\varpi_b\neq 0$ of the maximal ideal of $A_b$. Giving $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ its $k_0$-algebra structure through $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the assertion is: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $k_0$ and every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ with $W_0\cap k_0=A\cap k_0$, and every subring $B$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ carrying an $A_b$-algebra structure whose structure map is the inclusion, such that $B\subseteq W_0$, the image of $\varpi_b$ is prime in $B$, and $W_0$ consists of the ratios $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $\varpi_b\nmid h$, and such that for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$ for which $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$ is a domain and every index $\zeta\in\mathrm{Idx}\,q$ there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to the fixed field $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ of the scalar $C_s$-action on the Drinfeld function field with $\#C_s=2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$, $\ker\rho=(\varpi_b)$, $\rho$ inducing the residue map of $A$ on $A_b$, every element of $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ a ratio of values of $\rho$, the range of $\rho$ being exactly the part of the fixed field coming from $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$, and $\rho$ intertwining $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with the action of $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ on the Drinfeld function field — there exists $t\in W_0$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$ then every coefficient of $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   The conclusion says that the supersingular valuation ring $W_0$ is residually transcendental over $A\cap k_0$ in Deuring's sense: the residue of $t$ is transcendental over the residue field of the constants, so $W_0$ corresponds to a prime divisor of the reduction rather than to a point of the constant field. It is obtained from the affine Drinfeld chart of the supersingular component, and feeds the construction of the semistable model at supersingular places, being used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_affineChart) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_supersingularDVR_affineChart_of_levelField_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_supersingularDVR_affineChart_of_levelField_affineChart).
